# If you prefer the allow list template instead of the deny list, see community template:
# https://github.com/github/gitignore/blob/main/community/Golang/Go.AllowList.gitignore
#
# Binaries for programs and plugins
*.exe
*.exe~
*.dll
*.so
*.dylib

# Test binary, built with `go test -c`
*.test

# Output of the go coverage tool, specifically when used with LiteIDE
*.out

# Dependency directories (remove the comment below to include it)
# vendor/

# Go workspace file
go.work

# Program binaries
/ouroboros-mock
/gen-rollback-vector
# consensus/cmd/* binaries, when built to the repo root by a bare `go build`
/capture-sidecar
/compose-consensus-vector
/check-consensus-vector

# Working copy of the conformance corpus, extracted from the tracked archive
# conformance/blueprint-vectors.tar.gz by `make prepare-blueprint-testdata`.
# The archive, not this directory, is what ships in the Go module.
/conformance/testdata/eras/
